<title>INDIA: India pepper output seen at 65,000 T vs 62,000.</title>
<headline>India pepper output seen at 65,000 T vs 62,000.</headline>
<dateline>COONOOR, India 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Planters Association of Southern India (UPASI) has forecast Indian pepper production at 65,000 tonnes in 1996/97 (Nov-Oct) marginally higher than the record 62,000 tonnes achieved in the earlier year.</p>
<p>The forecast was presented at a planters' meeting being held in the southern Indian town of Coonoor.</p>
</text>
